WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.054 --> 00:00:03.957
Kaleem stared at Daisy in confusion.

2
00:00:03.958 --> 00:00:07.291
"Fireflies like the dark," Daisy said.

3
00:00:07.293 --> 00:00:11.332
"So do other nocturnal animals—like bats."

4
00:00:11.333 --> 00:00:15.624
"Right," Kaleem said. "That's why we're out here at night."

5
00:00:15.625 --> 00:00:21.791
"But . . ." Daisy waved a hand at the firepit and the houses surrounding them.

6
00:00:21.792 --> 00:00:25.457
"There's lots of light out here, even though it's nighttime.

7
00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:29.082
What if that's the reason the bats don't come out anymore?"

8
00:00:29.083 --> 00:00:34.332
Kaleem gasped. "Oh wow, that makes sense!

9
00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:38.892
I'll ask my parents to turn off the lights." He ran off.

10
00:00:38.893 --> 00:00:44.645
Daisy went inside and asked her father to put out the fire.

11
00:00:44.646 --> 00:00:48.830
"Can you turn off the outside lights on our house too?"

12
00:00:48.831 --> 00:00:56.416
Soon the two yards looked much darker.

13
00:00:56.417 --> 00:01:01.204
Kaleem bit his lip. "Do you think this will work? Will the bats come now?"

14
00:01:01.205 --> 00:01:06.580
"I don't know." Watching the fireflies, Daisy felt nervous.

15
00:01:06.581 --> 00:01:09.532
"The sky is definitely darker now.

16
00:01:09.533 --> 00:01:16.291
And there are lots of bugs here for them to eat."

17
00:01:16.292 --> 00:01:20.249
They sat down to wait again.

18
00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:23.457
Soon something flapped overhead.

19
00:01:23.458 --> 00:01:26.207
"Is that a bat?" Kaleem whispered.

20
00:01:26.208 --> 00:01:31.749
"No." Daisy was disappointed. "It's the owl again."

21
00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:34.292
She kept staring at the sky.

22
00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:37.012
"Maybe I was wrong," she thought.

23
00:01:37.013 --> 00:01:39.917
But she tried to sound hopeful for Kaleem.

24
00:01:39.918 --> 00:01:45.082
"We just have to keep waiting and see," Daisy said.

25
00:01:45.083 --> 00:01:51.978
It felt like forever. But suddenly something fluttered above the trees.

26
00:01:51.979 --> 00:01:54.637
"A bat!" Kaleem said.

27
00:01:54.638 --> 00:02:00.832
"Not just one!" Daisy said. "There's another one!"

28
00:02:00.833 --> 00:02:03.977
The friends grinned as more bats appeared.

29
00:02:03.978 --> 00:02:09.457
Kaleem took out his mom's phone.

30
00:02:09.458 --> 00:02:15.332
He snapped photo after photo.

31
00:02:15.333 --> 00:02:18.374
Daisy glanced at the fireflies.

32
00:02:18.375 --> 00:02:21.792
"I think there are more fireflies now too," she thought.

33
00:02:21.794 --> 00:02:25.957
"That gives me another idea!"

34
00:02:25.958 --> 00:02:28.958
Grace smiled shyly at the class.

35
00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:33.332
"And that's everything I learned about chipmunks!"

36
00:02:33.333 --> 00:02:37.154
"Well done, Grace," Mr. Neal said.

37
00:02:37.155 --> 00:02:40.262
"Next, two students will do their report together.

38
00:02:40.263 --> 00:02:42.535
Come on up, Daisy and Kaleem."

39
00:02:42.536 --> 00:02:46.863
The teacher switched off Grace's report on the whiteboard.

40
00:02:46.864 --> 00:02:49.582
Several new photos appeared.

41
00:02:49.583 --> 00:02:54.762
"I studied bats," Kaleem said. "Daisy studied fireflies."

42
00:02:54.763 --> 00:02:57.884
"They're both nocturnal animals," Daisy said.

43
00:02:57.885 --> 00:03:02.014
Kaleem nodded. "It wasn't easy to get these photos.

44
00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:06.041
Especially since there's a lot of light in our neighborhood."

45
00:03:06.042 --> 00:03:10.746
"Too much light can scare away or confuse animals," Daisy said.

46
00:03:10.747 --> 00:03:15.189
"It's called light pollution. And it can be bad for people too."

47
00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:20.957
She explained how fewer bats at night led to more mosquitoes bothering people.

48
00:03:20.958 --> 00:03:24.206
"That's because bats eat those insects."

49
00:03:24.207 --> 00:03:29.838
Mr. Neal nodded. "When I was growing up, this town stayed much darker at night.

50
00:03:29.839 --> 00:03:32.962
There were fewer stores and buildings.

51
00:03:32.963 --> 00:03:36.886
And most people didn't leave outdoor lights on all night."

52
00:03:36.887 --> 00:03:39.220
"Wow," someone murmured.

53
00:03:39.221 --> 00:03:43.624
"I'm going to ask my parents to turn our lights off earlier."

54
00:03:43.625 --> 00:03:46.166
"Me too!"

55
00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:48.666
"Great idea!"

56
00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:53.550
"Class, let's send an email to the town managers," Mr. Neal said.

57
00:03:53.551 --> 00:04:00.541
"I bet we can convince some local businesses to turn off some lights too."

58
00:04:00.542 --> 00:04:06.707
Daisy grinned, delighted that she'd solved the mystery of the missing bats.

59
00:04:06.708 --> 00:04:14.041
Outside, Beatrice buzzed against the window. She was delighted too.

60
00:04:14.042 --> 00:04:19.444
"Wait till I tell the council about Daisy's great work," Beatrice thought.

61
00:04:19.445 --> 00:04:27.235
"Daisy Dolittle is a [i@great@i] ambassador for animals!"

